=============================================================================

  | product_area_name | total_items |
  |-------------------|-------------|
  | Dairy             |      84,320 |
  | Bakery            |      71,905 |
  | Beverages         |      68,412 |

  Reading this result a grocery chain executive might conclude:
    1. Dairy is our highest-volume category — ensure premium shelf
       placement and negotiate volume discounts with dairy suppliers.
    2. Bakery is strong — consider in-store bakery expansion or
       cross-promotion with Dairy (cheese + bread bundles).
    3. Beverages sits 3rd — if a competitor dominates Beverages locally,
       a targeted promotion could win market share and boost overall spend.

  Each additional item sold per basket directly improves gross margin
  and reduces the per-customer cost of acquisition — both critical KPIs
  for sustainable profitability in the grocery sector.
=============================================================================
*/
